    "applicability": {
      "backend": "Debian bookworm OS packages of python:3.13.11-slim-bookworm. OpenSSL/glibc/gnutls are loaded by the Python runtime and its TLS clients; apt, dpkg and perl are not used at runtime.",
      "db": "Debian packages of postgres:17.11-bookworm and the Go stdlib of its gosu entrypoint helper; PostgreSQL is unpublished on the project network.",
      "https": "Caddy 2.10.2 and its Go modules terminate TLS for the loopback origin, plus Alpine OS packages; directly applicable to the HTTPS listener."
    },
    "disposition": "Unresolved for this candidate and recorded as a release gate item. Remediation requires refreshing the pinned bases (a newer python 3.13 slim patch, caddy 2.11.x and a newer PostgreSQL 17 patch), which changes the runtime, CI and lab images and needs the S1 build, install, upgrade and separation proof repeated. Exposure is limited to the loopback HTTPS origin and the private Compose network. Owner: E10 release gate (#13).",
